 "observable_mapping": "BETSE vm in this world is cell charge / (cm * sum mem_sa), uniform within a cell (Phi_b = 0; v_env not subtracted; sim.py:2029). Cells vm_ave = Q_cell / sum C_patch with C_patch = cm * mem_sa, broadcast to membranes for vm. Patch voltages and exterior potentials are diag_* arrays, reported only. Boundary-ring ECM sites are excluded: BETSE resets them each step, the resolved model holds them as reservoirs.",
 "notes": [
  "Reported only: venv_time (BETSE's screened, smoothed estimate has no Cells counterpart) and Cells diag_* arrays.",
  "Gate open fraction is not in the comparison layout and is not judged.",
  "Its judged run names this protocol (layouts carry their protocol's sha256); on CPU it repeats stage (i)'s Cells run bit for bit, only the reference differs.",
  "L4 variant (parity-l4-20261111-01): backend terms from the judged CPU run of physical_p2_barrier_direct_dense.json (/mnt/workspaces/Cells/parity-rung2-4-20261109-03/stage1/run/layout) and two blind L4 runs (/mnt/workspaces/Cells/parity-l4-20261111-01/blind-A/p2-barrier/run, /mnt/workspaces/Cells/parity-l4-20261111-01/blind-B/p2-barrier/run) from snapshot c819a4e41e5f61829ee604cfc3081f75408c0da2; the backend term also contains any engine difference between the two snapshots (the engine commits in between are recorded as leaving default trajectories unchanged).",
